  "recipe": {
    "technique": "The Hawaiian feather cloaks were decorated using yellow, red, sometimes black and green plumage taken from specific types of native birds (cf. § Bird feathers below). The plant used to make the netting is olonā or Touchardia latifolia, a member of the nettle family (cf. § Early and later types). Hundreds of thousands of feathers were required for each cloak. A small bundle of feathers (ʻuo or ʻuwo) was gathered and tied into the netting. Bundles were tied in close proximity to form a uniform covering of the surface of the cloak."
  },
